                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "93954588-64c0-3d66-a342-aa3a4b977068",
                        "entry_id": "ff080432-3f27-3488-b98b-9967012ec467",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ботан. травянистое растение семейства подорожниковых"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53e26a40-38d0-4913-ae5c-04f358433576",
                                "sense_id": "93954588-64c0-3d66-a342-aa3a4b977068",
                                "text": "В диком виде наперстянка пурпуровая растет только в Западной Европе, у нас же очень похожая на нее наперстянка с желтоватыми цветками часто встречается в лесах Кавказа и Южного Урала."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a20a71d-0708-4ddf-b50e-9cebf1af34bb",
                                "sense_id": "93954588-64c0-3d66-a342-aa3a4b977068",
                                "text": "У меня есть свои любимые цветы весной, среди них ― горная ромашка, колокольчик, наперстянка, дикий шиповник, распускающиеся березы и седой терн, которыми я любуюсь с неустанным восхищением."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7442aed3-98c5-4c82-ba21-ea4dae85c253",
                        "source_entry_id": "ff080432-3f27-3488-b98b-9967012ec467",
                        "source_sense_id": "93954588-64c0-3d66-a342-aa3a4b977068",
                        "target_lang_word": "foxglove",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foxglove",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d44030a8-1673-372d-a527-cb69b42a725d",
                                        "entry_id": "6fafb8f8-db10-308a-8f8c-bd69cab743ae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Digitalis, a genus of about 20 species of herbaceous biennials native to the Old World, certain of which are prized for their showy flowers. The drug digitalis or digoxin was first isolated from the plant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44c74cd3-0ade-4d19-893d-2929c76562cc",
                                                "sense_id": "d44030a8-1673-372d-a527-cb69b42a725d",
                                                "text": "Jemima alighted rather heavily, and began to waddle about in search of a convenient dry nesting-place. She rather fancied a tree-stump amongst some tall fox-gloves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a692d136-97b2-4a0f-82fa-b6309429bd07",
                                                "sense_id": "d44030a8-1673-372d-a527-cb69b42a725d",
                                                "text": "I wonder whether the witches would be wearing on their fingers their ornaments of foxglove blossoms, often called witches' bells or harebells, sometimes known as witches' thimbles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fda8608c-e404-4ed5-811b-285e13171e78",
                                                "sense_id": "d44030a8-1673-372d-a527-cb69b42a725d",
                                                "text": "There were bunches of wild garlic to keep out evil spirits, foxgloves for healing spells and hemlock and vervain for darker magic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
